{"id": "EUVD-2026-64545", "enisaUuid": "9dd8f66d-3263-35b8-9470-d74ca7eaf18e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: Fix use-after-free in cifs_try_adding_channels()\n\ncifs_try_adding_channels() takes a temporary reference to an interface\nbefore dropping iface_lock. If cifs_ses_add_channel() fails, it drops\nthat reference and then increments iface->weight_fulfilled.\n\nA concurrent interface list refresh can remove the list reference while\nchannel creation is in progress. In that case, the failure-path\nkref_put() releases the last reference and frees iface. Updating\nweight_fulfilled afterward then accesses freed memory.\n\nIncrement weight_fulfilled before dropping the temporary reference,\nkeeping iface alive for the final access.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:31:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:06:00", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64d7584e62ac8cdc750455c5fdc6008fc2de4f06", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c292d4686f717c03e5022fc4ae7c782f39a94915", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47dfac48bce7198ad4f1a388fc8c9491f878ac3b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ffacbadc14530e55b8d86f7b917524f6a0fb891", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1305eadc6a7d78a8d0a52eee29ddd2d9e8a27805", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4986410316b1ae0e63c6ce418e4eb196723626e7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74608", "GHSA-q727-xf93-53j5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d7b83d7-f639-3d51-8f4c-a51df1d9b799", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cff97d683a083b862a8bb24309e0f4d2d928128a <c292d4686f717c03e5022fc4ae7c782f39a94915"}, {"id": "270501ea-5a26-332b-8fef-ab27e3da2bf0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.152"}, {"id": "2a3a8668-966a-3d75-a1a9-9c7e284e08b6", "product": {"na